<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center" class="tborder" style="border-bottom: 0;">
	<tr class="titlebg">
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="15%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/topic/normal_post.gif" alt="" />
			Author
		</td>
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="85%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			Topic: When a guild loses its identity &nbsp;(Read 604 times)
		</td>
	</tr>
</table>
<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="bordercolor">
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=303" title="View the profile of Soupy Sales">Soupy Sales</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 90<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/opus1.jpg" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I&#039;m a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=303"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=666.msg5775#msg5775"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=666.msg5775#msg5775">When a guild loses its identity</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b> on:</b> February 26, 2004, 02:22:54 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I&#039;ve only played on two servers, obviously RN is one of them. I am amazed at the diversity of guilds on RN, but I do have a question?<br /><br />What happens when a guild, in order to advance, thinks it must change its core values or structure to do so? (ie. become a hardcore raiding guild instead of a casual raiding guild).<br /><br />Once you hit elemental do you need to implement mandatory raid requirements if you never needed them before? Do you need to restrict loot to certain classes if you never did before?<br /><br />Once you change into what the other guilds are, what do you do to keep your members happy? Why should i stay with a guild new to a certain level when I can jump ship and join one farther along? Certainly that elemental leather pattern i want is already rotting in XXX guild.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Prester John, 70 cleric, Dawning Nemesis<br /><br />Yes, I know, it&#039;s not the truth, but in a great history little truths can be altered so that the greater truth emerges.<br />-- Baudolino, Umberto Eco
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg5781"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=285" title="View the profile of Serepi">Serepi</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Guild Officer<br />
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 72<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://cfusionpm.com/misc/pulltoopen.gif" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								It&#039;s all about the tail, baby!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=285"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=666.msg5781#msg5781"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=666.msg5781#msg5781">Re:When a guild loses its identity</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #1 on:</b> February 26, 2004, 06:20:17 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Soupy Sales link=board=10;threadid=666;start=0#msg5775 date=1077823374</div><div class="quote"><br />Once you hit elemental do you need to implement mandatory raid requirements if you never needed them before? Do you need to restrict loot to certain classes if you never did before?</div><br />No one can answer that question for you. &nbsp;That&#039;s a question that you&#039;ll guild leadership will have to struggle with, debate, and come to a reasonable concensus on. &nbsp;There isn&#039;t a &quot;template&quot; out there - there is just too much diversity in personalities.<br /><br /><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Soupy Sales link=board=10;threadid=666;start=0#msg5775 date=1077823374</div><div class="quote">Once you change into what the other guilds are, what do you do to keep your members happy? Why should i stay with a guild new to a certain level when I can jump ship and join one farther along? Certainly that elemental leather pattern i want is already rotting in XXX guild.<br /></div><br />Again, no one can answer this for you. &nbsp;What I can speak to is what my own experiences are . &nbsp;You have to do what&#039;s fun. &nbsp;It&#039;s all about the process, not that attainment that makes it enjoyable. &nbsp;I have been part of the same guild for quite some time. &nbsp;We have gone the usual route of advancement (Kael HoT NToV limited Luclin stuff (ugh) and now PoP - currently elemental) and I couldn&#039;t imagine changing. &nbsp;No, we&#039;re not in Time. &nbsp;We will be, of that I&#039;m sure, but the fun is the *getting there* and knowing that I helped, in some small way, in building it. &nbsp;<br /><br />I could have jumped ship a couple of times and gone with more advanced guilds. &nbsp;I didn&#039;t. &nbsp;I won&#039;t. &nbsp;That&#039;s not fun, for me. &nbsp;What&#039;s fun for me is defeating the new encounters with the same core group of people that I&#039;ve been doing it with now since Kael. &nbsp;<br /><br />I think if you find yourself going to a new guild to get whatever loot and advance to new zones, and leave your friends behind, it&#039;ll be hollow victory for you. &nbsp;It would be for me. &nbsp;
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Serepi Serein<br />Officer, Hegemony Guild<br />&quot;Delenda est Carthago&quot;
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg5790"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=63" title="View the profile of Mordread">Mordread</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 37<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/spawn.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Guardian of the Crimson Flame<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=63"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:mordread_@hotmail.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=666.msg5790#msg5790"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=666.msg5790#msg5790">Re:When a guild loses its identity</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2 on:</b> February 27, 2004, 12:39:04 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Some people will stay with one guild because of loyalty. Some will stay because they like it there. Some will jump from guild to guild because they can never find a place that makes them happy and some will jump to any guild that is higher than the guild they are in at the moment. <br />The reasons for changing guilds are just about as many as the people who do it.<br /><br />As for what happenes when a guild reaches a certain point. Well.. a very few guilds manage to keep true to the path they set on upon creation. Most do not. In order to advance in PoP for instance you need people and gear. In order to get the gear you need a base of people who play and to get the base of people to play you usually have to advance most of the time. &nbsp;That is the killer for a lot of guilds, there are different people who want different things. That is one reason that you will see a lot of guilds splitting at some point or another. <br />If you look at how many guilds on Rodcet that have been around for 4+ years then you will find very very few. <br />The first thing you need to learn in a guild is that you will never ever be able to make everyone happy. It just wont happen. After a while a base usually forms of people who want more or less the same thing and those form the core of what the guild wants. Sometime it works and the guild moves on and prospers. Sometimes it doesn&#039;t work and the factions working against one another are too great and the guild splits or disbands. <br />So there isn&#039;t really any answer to your questions and there are a lot of answers. Funny thing that.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Mordread Draconius<br />Arch Convoker of Cascade Point
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg5799"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=3" title="View the profile of EQSysquella">EQSysquella</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								GO GO NERFED DPS<br />
								Guild Officer<br />
								Veeshan<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 1394<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.fotguild.com/vb3/image.php?u=27&amp;dateline=1085023518" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Grem&#039;s Parole Officer<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<a href="aim:goim?screenname=EQSysquella&amp;message=Hi.+Are+you+there?"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/aim.gif" alt="EQSysquella" border="0" /></a><br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=3"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=586624" title="Magelo" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
