							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=666.msg5799#msg5799"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=666.msg5799#msg5799">Re:When a guild loses its identity</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #3 on:</b> February 27, 2004, 05:20:48 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">o you need to restrict loot to certain classes if you never did before?<br /></div><br />Most guilds I know restrict BoW to war only.. Ifir to Rogue Only.. at the very least.. &gt;&lt;<br /><br />We have quite a few &quot;priority items&quot;. &nbsp;Just means thinking about a rare item that is the ultimate upgrade for a certain class listed where as the other classes would benefit- not as significant... &nbsp; 
						</td>
					</tr>
