	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg17726"></a><a name="new"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=303" title="View the profile of Soupy Sales">Soupy Sales</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 90<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/opus1.jpg" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I&#039;m a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=303"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=666.msg17726#msg17726"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=666.msg17726#msg17726">Re: When a guild loses its identity</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #5 on:</b> July 11, 2005, 05:23:10 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							18 months after I first posted this, I&#039;d like to comment on what I have learned.<br /><br />Stay true to your charter. If you are a family guild or a casual raiding guild (or a mix of the two), continue to recruit those that agree with you. If you must, merge with other guilds that feel the same way. <br /><br />If you are an officer or the guild leader of one of these guilds; I think it&#039;s best if you step aside and leave, rather than try to change the nature of your guild. Changing into a full time raid guild, should be left to the entire guild membership, not just the officers or leader.<br /><br />If you find yourself in a guild that has changed from its core values, feel free to search out a guild that is closer to what you like. Raiding 4+ hours 5-7 days a week can burn alot of people out. Its better to leave for a more casual environment than it is to burn out (quit) or flame out (burn all your bridges and old friends). Don&#039;t stick around until that happens.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Prester John, 70 cleric, Dawning Nemesis<br /><br />Yes, I know, it&#039;s not the truth, but in a great history little truths can be altered so that the greater truth emerges.<br />-- Baudolino, Umberto Eco
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
</table>
